    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Golden Hill began as a master‑planned community in January 1870, offering a sun‑kissed view just north of downtown San Diego.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://goldenhillcdc.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "For several decades, Golden Hill was the most fashionable place to live for the city’s affluent and middle class.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://goldenhillcdc.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1907 C Street estate, designed by city‑designated master builders Charles and Edward Quayle, remains a landmark of early Golden Hill architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://goldenhillcdc.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 25th Street Renaissance Project calms traffic, adds bike lanes, and encourages walking and public transit throughout Golden Hill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://goldenhillcdc.org/history/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Golden Hill’s streets showcase Victorian, Colonial Revival, Craftsman, and farmhouse homes, reflecting the neighborhood’s evolving architectural tastes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://goldenhillcdc.org/history/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Central Greater Golden Hill was mostly built‑out by the early 1920s, preserving a dense tapestry of historic homes.",
